SUMMARY:Weilflower Walk at Sugarloaf
DESCRIPTION:Join wildflower poet and Sugarloaf docent Phil Weil on this wildflower walk along Lower Bald Mountain and Meadow Trails. Meet outside the Visitor Center\, about 70 meters (250ft) past the entrance kiosk\, to the right. \nTickets are $10 for general audiences\, $5 for youth (12-17 year olds; all children under 18 must be accompanied by a parent or legal guardian)\, students\, Sugarloaf members\, and Sugarloaf or RFO volunteers\, and free for children under 12. \nWear comfortable shoes\, sun protection\, bring at least a quart of water\, and if desired\, a snack\, a camera\, and/or a wildflower identification guide. Parking fees apply; rains cancel.
URL:https://golocal.coop/event/weilflower-walk-at-sugarloaf-2/
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park\, 2605 Adobe Canyon Rd\, Kenwood\, CA
CATEGORIES:Kids and Family,Recreation
GEO:38.4427;-122.533
