SUMMARY:Pegasus Theater presents Push Back
DESCRIPTION:Distraught over what has been happening in the US since the current president took office\, Pegasus Theater Company members decided to do something theatrically creative to resist it. \nSo\, the Guerneville-based theater company put out a request for short plays related to the present US political climate\, and received 19 in less than two months. Four of these plays form the backbone of “Push Back\,” a production scheduled for April 17-19 and 24-26. It features these short plays by northern California playwrights\, along with a protest song sing-along that provides the audience with its own creative response to the madness. \nThese four freshly-minted plays portray the political landscape from both serious and absurdly comic perspectives. They include: “Executive Order”\, by L. H. Grant; “King Fear”\, by Thomas Graven and Lois Pearlman\, “X’ed”\, by Cary Pepper and “Tattoos”\, by Susan Sher. \nFriday and Saturday evenings the production begins at 7 p.m.\, and the Sunday matinees begin at 2 p.m. The doors open a half hour before curtain time. Admission is pay-what-you-will on both Friday evenings and reservations will not be taken. Admission is $20 on Saturdays and Sundays. \nAll performances will take place at the Mt. Jackson Masonic Lodge 14040 Church St. in downtown Guerneville. The entrance is around the corner on 3rd Street. \nAudience members can reserve tickets at pegasustheater2.eventbrite.com or purchase them at the door with cash or check. \nCome join in the experience. These resistance plays are irresistible.
URL:https://golocal.coop/event/pegasus-theater-presents-push-back/
LOCATION:Mt. Jackson Masonic Lodge\, 14040 Church Street\, Guerneville\, CA
CATEGORIES:Theater
GEO:38.5024;-122.999
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Mt. Jackson Masonic Lodge 14040 Church Street Guerneville CA;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=14040 Church Street:geo:-122.999,38.5024
END:VEVENT
